    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0532" n="442" xml:id="pg442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/3261</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-11-23T16:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">November 23,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>291. General Semenov now at Chita refuses
                    to acknowledge Admiral Kolchak’s
                    authority as dictator and is reported to have declared himself a dictator. He
                    has cut telegraph so we have now no communication beyond Chita.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Caldwell</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
